After accepting the repository input by its hash and ELF contract, the APK
builder compiles the AGENTCODI C++ policy guard and injects that one guard as a
DT_NEEDED dependency with pinned build-only patchelf 0.19.1. A relocation-free
AGENTCODI C++ attestor is then placed in its own 16-KiB-aligned read/execute
PT_LOAD segment, using a redundant PT_NOTE program-header slot while preserving
the original Android-note bytes in their existing load. The ELF entry first
checks that the genuine no-follow sibling guard's device and inode are the ones
mapped executable; only then does it continue to ripgrep's original entry. This
prevents LD_LIBRARY_PATH substitution from suppressing the guard constructor.
The builder accepts only the intermediate, payload, guard, final, and exact
dependency hashes above. Neither the input nor the packaged runtime is
downloaded, installed, rebuilt, modified, or repaired at Android runtime.

