Verification results
--------------------
Both the repository input and guarded APK runtime report ripgrep 15.2.0,
`features:-pcre2`, and NEON support through `rg --version`.
`rg --pcre2-version` reports that PCRE2 is unavailable and exits nonzero.
The target-specific Cargo normal-dependency closure contains exactly 34
packages and contains neither pcre2 nor pcre2-sys. The complete closure,
source checksums, selected license files, Rust standard-library input, LLVM
link input, and Android dynamic dependencies are recorded in DEPENDENCIES.
No absolute project or Termux build-host path remains in either ripgrep ELF.
Remapped `/usr/src/ripgrep-15.2.0` and `/usr/src/cargo` diagnostic source paths
remain. The guard enforces activation, argument filtering, environment cleanup,
and the canonical executable entry point before ripgrep's own entry point can
run, including for an absolute invocation of the APK-native ELF. The in-binary
attestor additionally rejects a substituted guard before ripgrep's original
entry can run.
